  "preamble": "Complete loss of the velar ejective. In Boni (Sam, Cushitic), Proto-East-Cushitic *kʼ (via Proto-Sam *q) was lost word-initially and became ʔ after vowels (Heine 1978); Afar and Bayso each show initial loss in a single etymology in Ehret (1991). In Dogrib (Athabaskan), stem-final back ejectives were dropped together with the development of low tone.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Elision, Debuccalization",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
